## 6. Residual (not this cycle)

  These facts stay residual. They are not `[ ]` work unless the owner names one.
  Public first-machine install is the host script at `https://openooda.org/install` (Linux x86_64). `ooda install` remains the checkout XDG copy after you already have `ooda`. ARM / macOS / Windows packs stay open above.
  HITL is not product. The human loop is `ooda fix`.
  vscode launches `ooda lsp`. `vscode/server/ooda-lsp.js` remains on disk and is residual.
  `qa/e2e/*.sh` and the broken fixtures named in the `qa_master.oo` header stay residual. `qa_master.oo` is product (22 green).
  `import ".h"` still refuses. `import_c(...)` and `lto_xlang_link` are product (OPEN-70).
  AArch64 product-ELF dispatch is residual. Side emit-aarch64 hello/const-if .s + clang assemble is a named lock (`scripts/aarch64_*_smoke.oo`). Link and qemu run stay residual. Standalone x86_64 `emit-x86` is product (OPEN-69).
  Dummy WASM `end` stays on non-print functions. Print-lit, hello greet fold, same-fn ident-let, N-string const strcat, two-println, three-println, int-lit println, const INT+INT, if-true/if-false, if-true-no-else, if INT==INT, if INT!=INT, if-false-no-else, four-println, five-println, six-println, seven-println, const else-if, INT+INT+INT, INT-INT, INT*INT, INT/INT, INT%INT, unary-minus println, bool true/false println, if INT<INT, if INT>INT, if INT<=INT, if INT>=INT, if !true/!false, and if BOOL&&BOOL are named locks. Mixed ident concat stays dummy. Hostile second print stays dummy. IDENT if stays dummy. IDENT add stays dummy. IDENT third/fourth/fifth/sixth/seventh print, extra stmt beside no-else, if 1==x, if 1!=x, if 1<x, if 1>x, if 1<=x, if 1>=x, if !x, if true&&x, non-const else-if, IDENT in add3, IDENT sub, IDENT mul, IDENT div, IDENT mod, IDENT unary-minus, and IDENT bool stay dummy. Extra emit-wasm writes `\0asm`. A browser WASM host is residual. Not a complete WASM backend.
  Device GPU dispatch is residual. `emit_ptx` text is product (OPEN-91).
  SGX / TDX / SEV hardware enclaves are residual. Measured isolate is product (OPEN-74).
